            <title>0.8.6</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:13:00 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1793653830</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Changed

- The app icon now ships as an Icon Composer asset, so macOS 26 and later mask it correctly instead of drawing it inside a grey frame.

## Fixed

- **Selection**
  - Word and line drag selections stay on the right text when the view scrolls during the drag, and keep their word or line steps while a drag autoscrolls past the top or bottom edge.
  - A selection is now cleared when the app could change the text under it: a switch between the primary and alternate screen, a forwarded right click, or an app repaint under a Shift-drag selection while mouse tracking is on.
  - The caret, mouse hits and selection now line up with the drawn text when one pane fills a view whose height is not a whole number of pixels.
- **Split panes**
  - Panes below or beside a divider can shrink to the minimum size. Only the top panes reserve room for the titlebar strip.
  - When an outer divider moves, every pane of a nested split in the same direction stays at or above the minimum size.
  - VoiceOver pane splitters keep working after each step and after the window moves, and they announce each step right away.
- **Sessions**
  - A tab that loses its session lease gets it back, so it keeps accepting keystrokes.
  - Restoring or opening a session never replaces a session that is still running. If Laban cannot look up the session, it reports an error instead of starting a new session over it.
  - Clients that connect at the same time can no longer leave a session's state half-updated, and an older request can no longer overwrite newer session state.
- **Terminal**
  - When no colors are configured, Laban now answers every color query in a chained OSC 10/11/12 request, not only the first. Each reply ends with the same terminator as the query (BEL or ST).
- **Command line**
  - A misspelled flag such as `--jsno` now fails with an error. Before, the command ran as if the flag was not there. `--` ends option parsing on all subcommands.
- **Agent proxy**
  - A slow control request no longer kills the agent. If the upstream connection is lost or answers late, the proxy returns 502 and never sends a late reply to the wrong request.
]]></description>
